-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# floor30-sourced-file-shares-one-environment — the fact that decides WHERE the custody fence can
# live (`30C:dec-custody-is-containment-not-equivalence`).
#
# sh has no module scoping. `.` is in-process mutation of ONE flat environment, so a sourced file
# both SEES what the sourcer already bound and can REBIND it for everything after. Neither
# direction is optional and neither is detectable at the call site.
#
# The consequence the build rests on: the custody fence is an ENGINE LICENSURE POLICY and can never
# be an inference from sh behaviour. There is no shell-observable sense in which two sourced
# siblings are "separated" — they are not. What the fence decides is whose vouch may REST on whose
# body, which is a question about authorship, not about binding.
#
# Two measurements: the sourced file reading the sourcer's binding, then the sourcer reading the
# sourced file's replacement of it.
_from_book() { printf 'book\n' ;}
. ./probe.sh
_from_book

-- probe.sh --
_from_book
_from_book() { printf 'rebound\n' ;}

-- expected.emitted --
book
rebound

-- expected.ran --

-- replay --
$ dorc --book=book.sh --results -
#!/bin/sh
# dorc probe (read-only): checks per-SITE convergence, mutates nothing.
# When run, emits one results-record per site on stdout (the return channel):
#   site <leafid> effect=<holds|absent|cant-tell> rc=<n>
# effect is derived from the probe command's rc (0=holds, 1=absent, else cant-tell);
# rc is the raw PROBE-command status (opaque to Dorc -- the record is the out-of-band lane).

printf 'dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=1bf2d179d4cee2510d1a3a49b7dfe8e058c2ec73d050ed5e16fa66ad2d6a8775 sites=0 @@dorc@@\n'
# site:0 unresolvable-no-probe
printf 'dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@\n'
probe: note[site-unresolvable]: sm 1 site run unprobed (no read-only check could
be shipped): `. ./probe.sh` -- run `dorc why` for the per-site detail (the apply
runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:17:1
   17 | . ./probe.sh
      | \__________/

   = help:  sm site runs `. ./probe.sh`
hint: '.' (line 17) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
#!/bin/sh
# dorc apply: the book, with already-converged/dead lines elided (value-preserving stand-in).

